# Input
```ts
/* should generate diagnostics */
async function f1() { return await (1 as number); }
async function f2() { return await ([1, 2]!); }
async function f3() { return await ([1, 2] as const); }
async function f4() { return await ([1, 2] satisfies number[]); }
// No fix: without `await`, these would start a declaration.
async function f5() { await function () {}!; }
async function f6() { await class {}!; }

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.ts:2:30 lint/nursery/noUselessAwait  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This value is never a promise, so await is unnecessary.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ async function f1() { return await (1 as number); }
      │                              ^^^^^
    3 │ async function f2() { return await ([1, 2]!); }
    4 │ async function f3() { return await ([1, 2] as const); }
  
  i Awaiting a value that isn't a promise returns the same value, but still delays the code that follows it.
  
  i Remove await. To wait for several promises, pass them to Promise.all() instead.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Remove await.
  
    2 │ async·function·f1()·{·return·await·(1·as·number);·}
      │                              ------                

